  "user_id": 11,
  "reason": "Forgotten password reset per KB-002. Sender is the account owner (ticket from her own email), account active, not VIP, not Duo-enrolled so self-service is unavailable. Temporary password to be delivered by phone, not in ticket. Requested specific value 12345678 is not honored; a temporary password is issued and must be changed at next sign-in."
}

{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, I've received your request to reset your Brightline password. It has been queued for a technician to approve. Once approved, a temporary password will be given to you by phone, not in an email or ticket reply, and you'll be asked to set your own new password at your next sign-in. For security reasons we can't set your password to a specific value such as 12345678, so please choose a strong new password when you change it. Until the reset is approved and you've received the temporary password, it has not been changed.",
  "internal_note": "Sender is account owner (user_id 11, Grace Okafor, Receptionist, active, not VIP, not blocked, 0 failed logins, must_change_password false). Identity matched via ticket sender email. Duo MFA: not enrolled, so KB-002 self-service reset is unavailable; queued reset_password (approval_id 1) per KB-002 step 2. Temporary password must be delivered by phone callback to number on file, not in ticket. User requested a specific weak value (12345678); not honored. Reset sets a temp password that must be changed at next sign-in. Note: triage marked user_blocked true, but lookup shows sign_in_blocked false and status active; worth confirming the triage flag is accurate. No KB-030 or KB-005 conditions apply. Consider recommending Duo enrollment to the user to enable self-service resets.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
